# Stroke program — the compact animation blob the Blender encoder emits and
# the RISC-V guest executes over ENet. Rung 0 of the stroked-drawing surface:
# the wire format for integer channels (tip x/y/z, press depth, tilt, side,
# time step), zigzag-delta-encoded per channel and packed into fixed-size
# 512-bit packets with a keyframe every N rows.
#
# SOURCE OF TRUTH — the Lean spec in `2-contract/drawing-lean` is the
# acceptance criteria. The theorems the stub generator must make hold:
#   packet_roundtrip, run_conserves, same_packets_same_order, heals_within.
#
# Format: one declaration per line, `#` comments, `Class.method(args) -> Ret`.
# The same role as `godot_sandbox_syscalls.sigs` (guest ECALLs) and
# `cloth_fit_usd.sigs`/`weftfit_retarget.sigs` (C ABI the host links).
#
# ---- zigzag deltas ---------------------------------------------------
StrokeCodec.zig(x) -> Nat                          # zigzag delta to a natural code
StrokeCodec.unzig(n) -> Int                        # code back to a signed delta
StrokeCodec.encode(n, c, prev, ss) -> Packet       # up to `n` samples after prev into a 512-bit packet
StrokeCodec.decode(prev, k) -> List (List Int)     # packets into the same samples, bit for bit

# ---- keyframe row codec (N rows = 1 keyframe) -------------------------
StrokeChain.encRows(N, i, p, rows) -> List Nat     # keyframe row = absolute, else delta from previous row
StrokeChain.decRows(N, c, i, p, codes) -> List (List W)   # rebuild the rows, keyframe row resets prev

# ---- self-healing (row i % N == 0 => prev ignored) --------------------
StrokeHeal.encKF(N, c, i, p, ss) -> List (List Nat)  # encode rows against zero at keyframes
StrokeHeal.decKF(N, c, i, p, rows) -> List (List Int)  # decode; prev ignored at keyframe rows

# ---- ordering (co-presence: HLC + pen stamp) --------------------------
# A packet's stamp is the fabric HLC advance plus a unique pen id; stamps
# are strictly increasing per pen. Clients holding the same packets apply
# them in the same order whatever order they arrived in.
StrokeOrder.stamp(clock, pen) -> Stamp             # stamp a packet: HLC advance + pen id
StrokeOrder.applyOrder(packets) -> packets         # mergeSort by stamp; same multiset, always ordered
